 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- Tool input is now validated against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before its executor runs.
+  Input the schema rejects (a missing `required` property, a wrong type, a value outside an `enum`)
+  comes back to the model as a tool result naming the failing property path and the constraint,
+  never the offending value, so the model can correct the call; the executor is not invoked.
+  Extra properties pass through unmodified. An executor that used to hand-validate its input now
+  receives only input the schema already accepts. `ToolRegistry.register` throws, naming the tool,
+  when a static schema cannot be compiled. `execute` still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`.
+
